# --- PII / campaign-data guard (added 2026-08-26) ---
# The policy at the top of this file already says campaign data must never enter
# the repo, but the patterns enforcing it were incomplete: research-exclude.csv
# (1575 real contact email addresses) and the followup-state.sqlite3 family were
# untracked AND unignored, so a single  would have published them.
# Generalised from literal filenames to patterns so new files are covered too.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
*-exclude.csv
research-exclude.csv
personalizations*.csv

# --- blanket CSV guard (added 2026-08-26) ---
# The rules above name specific files. This repo holds 1575 real contact records,
# so a NEW export under an unanticipated name would still be committable.
# Deny all CSV by default; allow back only the vetted public-domain blocklist.
*.csv
*.CSV
!enterprise-exclusions.csv
